@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cookie Policy - LinkedLearn";
}

<section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-slate-50 min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-6">Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-slate-500 mb-12">Last updated: @DateTime.Now.ToString("MMMM dd, yyyy")</p>
        
        <div class="prose prose-slate lg:prose-lg max-w-none text-slate-700 space-y-8">
            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">What Are Cookies?</h2>
                <p>Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer or mobile device when you visit a website. They are widely used to make websites work, or work more efficiently, as well as to provide information to the owners of the site.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">How We Use Cookies</h2>
                <p>LinkedLearn uses cookies and similar local storage technologies for the following purposes:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong>Authentication & Security:</strong> We use cookies to store your secure session so that you remain logged in as you navigate through courses, your dashboard, and checkout pages.</li>
                    <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> To remember your preferences, such as your selected category filters, theme choices, or shopping cart items before checkout.</li>
                    <li><strong>Performance & Analytics:</strong> To understand how you use our platform, which helps us improve the user experience and optimize our systems.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Managing Your Cookies</h2>
                <p>Most web browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings preferences. However, if you limit the ability of websites to set cookies, you may worsen your overall user experience, since it will no longer be personalized to you. It may also stop you from saving customized settings like login information.</p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
